    {
      "x": 18,
      "y": 0,
      "dx": 0,
      "dy": 1,
      "title": "A SHIFT REPORT",
      "text": "Third shift. Forty blocks of red stone cut from the new face. The stone is warm when it comes out, and colder every hour after. Two men put their hands on it to warm them and would not take them off again. They were sent up to the castle with the blocks."
    },
    {
      "x": 20,
      "y": 9,
      "dx": 1,
      "dy": 0,
      "title": "HALE'S NOTEBOOK: DAY 6",
      "text": "The mine goes deeper than any map of it. At the bottom a seam of the red stone runs through the rock like a vein, and it beats, slowly, about once an hour. I timed it against my watch. It beats in time with the numbers."
    }
